 I noticed the same thing... When I used my original 2.4.39 kernel from
RH/Compaq, the speeds were actually faster than if I used the 2.6.x kerns
from kernel.org... With some tweaking with HDPARM and a later kernel,
2.6.11.6, the speed picked back up. I also did some checking around and
found the specs for the drives, two 18gb SCSI II Quantums, their max output
was something like 11MBs and that was right were I was at with tweaking. The
only problem with HDPARM and SCSI is everything is set by the drive and
there's little HDPARM can do to get around it.

I also noticed the same thing with my UDMA drives, same as with the SCSI, a
little tweaking with HDPARM and a newer kernel, and were running like a
top... went from a mopey 12MB to around 26-29MBs.  Will L G

